  "notes": "Unit = GRCh38 novel junction of arm A, labelled by where the SAME reads splice on the personal genome. T = same-canonical (non-canonical on GRCh38) + shifted-known + unspliced; T_core drops unspliced (short introns that minimap2 renders as a deletion on the diploid assembly, median 82 bp; 308/499 of B2's are spliced on the SNV genome B1). R_rule = junctions meeting the rescue's own criterion (what the axis sees); R = junctions inside isoforms that got the REFERENCE_BIAS verdict (needs ALL of the isoform's novel junctions explained, NIC/NNC only). The gap R_rule -> R (35 -> 13) is the all-junctions rule and the category pass-throughs, not the motif criterion. Precision misses (4/35) are junctions whose reads come from the non-canonical haplotype. Firewall: 0 rescues under unknown provenance, 18/18 held.",
